WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.740
Kevin Costner plays a stern but noble leader
in "Yellowstone" – but how does he treat

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.590
the show's cast and crew in real life?

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.349
"Yeah?"

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:16.090
Among the band of tough nuts wandering around
in worn-down denim and cowboy hats in Taylor

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.380
Sheridan's "Yellowstone," none can hold a
candle to Kevin Costner's John Dutton.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.199
Patriarch of the modern-day Dutton family,
head of the family business, and forceful

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.119
overseer of his children's various enterprises,
John Dutton is a man who routinely makes it

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:31.869
clear he is not one to be trifled with lightly.

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:36.300
Given such an effortlessly tough exterior,
it only seems natural for audiences to wonder...

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.780
Just how much of John Dutton comes from the
two-time Academy Award-winning star's real

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.840
personality?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.129
Ryan Bingham, the actor who plays Walker on
the Emmy-nominated series, might have a potentially

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:48.100
interesting perspective on the matter.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.960
In "Yellowstone," Walker is portrayed as the
odd man out among the various ranch hands

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.590
on the Dutton Yellowstone Ranch.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.309
In fact, in Season 2, a particularly nasty
encounter with John Dutton's right-hand man,

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:01.260
Rip Wheeler, nearly results in Walker's untimely
demise.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.120
So, how does Bingham feel about Costner in
real life?

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.310
And, perhaps even more importantly, do the
rest of the "Yellowstone" cast ever find themselves

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.689
on the receiving end of John Dutton's signature
menacing stare?

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.630
Thankfully, the cast and crew of "Yellowstone"
have offered information about Costner that

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:20.750
paints the actor in a decidedly different
manner than that of his stoic on-screen counterpart.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.150
As viewers might have hoped, it doesn't take
long to realize that Costner's "Yellowstone"

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.479
persona is firmly confined to the boundaries
of the small screen.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.640
In a wide-ranging interview with the Los Angeles
Times released in February, Bingham covered

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.350
a variety of interesting topics related to
himself and his job on the set of "Yellowstone."

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:41.060
Unsurprisingly, he also had good things to
say about his on-screen and off-screen boss.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.140
Bingham revealed that despite John Dutton's
tense nature, the seasoned star behind the

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.979
character is actually a legitimate joy to
be around.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:52.360
In fact, Bingham shared one particular detail
about Costner's on-set behavior that makes

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.530
him a true standout in Hollywood.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.590
According to Bingham, Costner insists that
he shake the hand of each and every cast and

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.130
crew member every day.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:04.790
Of course, although John Dutton also seems
like a handshake type of guy, most characters

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.980
on the series can never be totally sure that
the hand being offered by Dutton isn't also

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.440
gripping a revolver.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.120
While many could likely have guessed it, it's
surely a relief to recognize that Costner

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.750
isn't quite so tightly wound up as the character
he portrays.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:22.310
As the leading man of the series (and an executive
producer too), Costner's behavior on the set

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.800
surely lays down a tone for the rest of the
cast and crew to follow.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.300
According to Bingham, people on the set of
"Yellowstone" often feel the freedom to lighten

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.290
the mood once the job is done for the day
and the camera is turned off.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.330
Bingham said in the interview,

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.790
"We're always joking backstage and things
like that.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.420
It's interesting how light and fun it is when
we're on set and we're playing around.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.020
People are chasing around horses and things
like that.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.170
But then when you see the show, it can be
pretty dark."

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.320
Despite the noted difference between the series
and real life, one particularly interesting

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.230
aspect that connects the two is Bingham's
penchant for playing the guitar.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.340
Although Lloyd doesn't take too kindly to
Walker's melodies in Season 4, the real-life

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.420
crew appears to like it quite a bit.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.340
During a conversation released by Paramount
Network as a "Yellowstone" bonus feature,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.730
a number of "Yellowstone" cast members noted
Bingham's regular use of the guitar on set.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:12.170
Ian Bohen, the actor who plays Ryan, said
that Bingham plays the guitar "constantly,"

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.280
something everyone seems to enjoy.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.100
"He pulls out a guitar, and he'll just get
off in his own world.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:20.042
And everyone stops what they're doing... and
just listens to it.

00:03:20.042 --> 00:03:21.430
It's a dream."

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.900
Given all the camaraderie on set in the real
world, perhaps the perennially stressed Dutton

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.710
clan could benefit from taking a short trip
out to the bunkhouse too?

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:33.060
Maybe they'll get the chance when Paramount
Network begins airing "Yellowstone" Season

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.380
5 at some point later this year.

